cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ROOT I/O Specification
message: >-
  If you use this specification or its reference files, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andres
    family-names: Rios Tascon
    alias: ariostas
repository-code: https://github.com/ariostas/root-io-spec
url: https://ariostas.github.io/root-io-spec/
abstract: >-
  A specification of the ROOT on-disk binary formats -- the container layer,
  object serialization, the classes whose recorded streamer information does not
  describe their bytes, and TTree -- written so that a third party can implement
  a reader without reading ROOT's C++ source. It is written by an AI agent from
  ROOT's source under human direction, which is tractable only because every claim
  is verified twice by machine: against a pinned ROOT release with a path:line
  citation, and against real bytes in a committed reference file. The invariants
  of each layer run over 252 ROOT files this project did not write.
keywords:
  - ROOT
  - TFile
  - TTree
  - RNTuple
  - binary format
  - file format specification
  - high energy physics
  - serialization
# The prose is CC-BY-4.0 and the tools, generators and reference files are
# BSD-3-Clause; LICENSE says which is which.
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - BSD-3-Clause
license-url: https://github.com/ariostas/root-io-spec/blob/main/LICENSE
# The specification tracks ROOT rather than carrying a meaning of its own, so its
# releases are CalVer (YYYY.MM.DD), tagged at a milestone. Bumping these two lines
# is part of cutting one. 0.1.0 was the last release under the old scheme.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-17'
